	Another danger in this case if UWEC loses a lawsuit against McElwaine
is that it probably will result in many sites revoking posting capabilities
altogether,  probably including UWEC itself.  I mean,  if a site cannot do
something about a person who is a serious problem poster,  it probably will
have to take net access away from everybody.  Yes,  I place a very high value
on free speech,  but McElwaine's distribution tactics are clearly abusive:
posting long monologues on ~ALL~ newsgroups without any concern to
appropriateness.  I mean,  the man was a human roboposter.

	A challenge USENET has ahead of itself is how it can enfore it's own
rules.  USENET is an anarchy,  so it doesn't have formal rules;  however,
everyone on USENET has some idea of what those rules should be,  and people
who do things that are far from the consensus are going to get their sysadmin
bombed with mail.  In an anarchy,  there isn't really any other way to do
this,  although if someone really wants,  they can vote with sendsys bombs,
other kinds of mail and news exclusion attacks,  fists or guns.  One hopes
that those people will bring down the wrath of the community.

	However,  the fact that the individual sysadmin is responsible for
applying sanctions to users,  means that the policy is going to vary from
site to site.  It is the ultimate example of "state's rights",  and as much
as I like regional autonomy and diversity,  I really hate the way things like
this inevitably create differences in rules that lead to unfairness and
give advantages to the rich,  the big,  and the criminal.  The moral:  USENET
needs to police itself,  to prevent the police from doing it for us.  If
Mcelwaine-vs-UWEC is decided in the favor of McElwaine,  many .edu sites,
and possibily others,  are going to shut down the posting abilities of ALL
users,  as this is the only way they will be able to defend themselves
against McElwaine and his peers.  So,  the people who are talking about
defending McElwaine will be really happy with themselves,  hell,  they might
lose their own ability to post as a result.



